  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Elimination of Mother-to-child-transmission of HIV (EMTCT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The MOH has called for the elimination of mother-to-child-transmission of HIV (EMTCT) to be considered a high priority in the overall fight against HIV. To address these ongoing challenges, the activity has three main objectives:  1. provide technical assistance to health facilities to increase access to quality comprehensive child-centered health services  2. strengthen national policies and systems to improve c/alhiv outcomes  3. sustain quality hiv and tb services.</narrative>
  </description>
